{"issue": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2111", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2111/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2111/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2111/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2111", "id": 1844052560, "node_id": "I_kwDOBabE0s5t6gJQ", "number": 2111, "title": "ArduPilot - Possibility of using MAV_CMD_DO_SET_SERVO instead of MAV_CMD_DO_SET_ACTUATOR", "user": {"login": "trolledbypro", "id": 57928210, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU3OTI4MjEw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57928210?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro", "html_url": "https://github.com/trolledbypro", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/trolledbypro/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 1594597435, "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWwxNTk0NTk3NDM1", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/labels/feature", "name": "feature", "color": "2be2be", "default": false, "description": ""}], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 5, "created_at": "2023-08-09T21:35:17Z", "updated_at": "2024-05-27T09:25:16Z", "closed_at": "2024-05-27T09:25:15Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI've been messing around with the set-actuator example with my WSL2 ArduPilot SITL. I have seen that the set_actuator function is causing an unsupported message to appear in my terminal. Upon investigation of the source code: https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/fadfe22e7c053945107201e2638be9a7f8b8ee5c/src/mavsdk/plugins/action/action_impl.cpp#L516-L550\r\nI see that MAV_CMD_DO_SET_ACTUATOR is being used to only set _one_ actuator to a specific value. This command is unsupported in ArduPilot (indicated by it's absence in [this list](https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/mavlink-other-commands.html#mav-cmds))\r\n\r\nIn theory, we could use MAV_CMD_DO_SET_SERVO to accomplish what MAV_CMD_DO_SET_ACTUATOR is doing in ArduPilot.\r\nHowever, I am not sure if MAV_CMD_DO_SET_ACTUATOR is supported in PX4 (https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/pull/15281).\r\n\r\nWould it be more preferable to change the set_actuator function to use MAV_CMD_DO_SET_SERVO or to implement a switch statement that implements MAV_CMD_DO_SET_SERVO if the AP is found to be using ArduPilot?\r\nI could attempt to implement a case such as this: https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/fadfe22e7c053945107201e2638be9a7f8b8ee5c/src/mavsdk/plugins/action/action_impl.cpp#L658-L670\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_u